name iana-language-subtag-registry
# The IANA language subtag registry (RFC 5646, 3.1): records of fields, parted by a line "%%"; each field written
# "Field-Name: value", a line that begins with white space continuing the one before. A record is about its Subtag, or
# its Tag (a grandfathered or redundant tag has a Tag and no Subtag); every other field is said of it as RFC 5646
# words what the field means. The first record holds only the File-Date: it is said of the file, in its metadata.
# The file does not name who publishes it; the directory it is kept in is named iana.
match language-subtag-registry.txt
witness {dir}

tier record by \n%%\n
tier field by \n
is :
continued

thing record Subtag
thing record Tag
metadata File-Date
omit Added Deprecated
content *
# Type and Scope are values of the registry's own lists. RFC 5646:
#   3.1.3: "The field 'Type' contains the string identifying the record type in which it appears." ("language",
#          "extlang", "script", "region", "variant", "grandfathered", "redundant")
#   3.1.11: "The field 'Scope' contains classification information about a primary or extended language subtag
#          derived from ISO 639." ("macrolanguage", "collection", "special", "private-use")
value - Type Scope
#   3.1.5: "The field 'Description' contains a description of the tag or subtag in the record."
relation "a description of the tag or subtag in the record" Description
#   3.1.7: "The field 'Preferred-Value' contains a mapping between the record in which it appears and another tag or subtag."
relation "a mapping between the record in which it appears and another tag or subtag" Preferred-Value
#   3.1.8: "The field 'Prefix' contains a valid language tag that is RECOMMENDED as one possible prefix to this
#          record's subtag, perhaps with other subtags."
relation "one possible prefix to this record's subtag" Prefix
#   3.1.9: "This field indicates a script used to write the overwhelming majority of documents for the given language"
relation "a script used to write the overwhelming majority of documents for the given language" Suppress-Script
#   3.1.10: "This field indicates a language that encompasses this subtag's language according to assignments made by ISO 639-3."
relation "a language that encompasses this subtag's language" Macrolanguage
#   3.1.12: "The field 'Comments' contains additional information about the record"
relation "additional information about the record" Comments
attest record *
